### ============================================================
###  STUDENT API — Online Learning Platform
###  Base URL : http://localhost:1935/student-api
###  Auth     : Bearer token — login as STUDENT first via POST /auth/login
###             then set: Authorization: Bearer <token>
### ============================================================

### ── COURSES (BROWSE) ─────────────────────────────────────────

### [1] Browse All Active Courses
###     Returns all courses where isCourseActive === true.
###     Used on the course catalogue / browse page.
GET http://localhost:1935/student-api/courses
Authorization: Bearer <token>

###

### ── PAYMENT ───────────────────────────────────────────────────
###  Calling /pay automatically creates the enrollment record.
###  You do NOT need to call /enroll separately for new enrollments.
###  /enroll is kept for edge-cases (e.g. manual admin re-enrollment).

### [2] Pay for a Paid Course (UPI example)
###     transactionId must be globally unique (idempotency key).
###     On success, enrollment is created and wishlist entry is removed.
POST http://localhost:1935/student-api/pay
Content-Type: application/json
Authorization: Bearer <token>

{
    "course": "684a2c3d5e6f7a8b9c0d1e2f",
    "amount": 999,
    "method": "UPI",
    "transactionId": "TXN-20250609-ARJUN-JAVA-001",
    "status": "SUCCESS"
}

###

### [3] Pay via Card
POST http://localhost:1935/student-api/pay
Content-Type: application/json
Authorization: Bearer <token>

{
    "course": "684a2c3d5e6f7a8b9c0d1e2f",
    "amount": 1499,
    "method": "CARD",
    "transactionId": "TXN-20250609-ARJUN-REACT-002",
    "status": "SUCCESS"
}

###

### [4] Pay via Net Banking
POST http://localhost:1935/student-api/pay
Content-Type: application/json
Authorization: Bearer <token>

{
    "course": "684a2c3d5e6f7a8b9c0d1e2f",
    "amount": 799,
    "method": "NET_BANKING",
    "transactionId": "TXN-20250609-ARJUN-PY-003",
    "status": "SUCCESS"
}

###

### [5] Pay via Wallet
POST http://localhost:1935/student-api/pay
Content-Type: application/json
Authorization: Bearer <token>

{
    "course": "684b3d4e5f6a7b8c9d0e1f3a",
    "amount": 499,
    "method": "WALLET",
    "transactionId": "TXN-20250609-ARJUN-DS-004",
    "status": "SUCCESS"
}

###

### [6] Enroll in a Free Course (method = "FREE", amount = 0)
###     FREE was added to the PaymentModel enum to support zero-cost courses.
POST http://localhost:1935/student-api/pay
Content-Type: application/json
Authorization: Bearer <token>

{
    "course": "684c4e5f6a7b8c9d0e1f2a3b",
    "amount": 0,
    "method": "FREE",
    "transactionId": "TXN-FREE-20250609-ARJUN-HTML-005",
    "status": "SUCCESS"
}

###

### ── ENROLLMENT (MANUAL) ───────────────────────────────────────
###  NOTE: /pay already creates the enrollment automatically.
###  Use /enroll only when you need to manually link an existing payment
###  to an enrollment (e.g., after a payment gateway callback).

### [7] Manual Enroll (requires an existing Payment ID)
POST http://localhost:1935/student-api/enroll
Content-Type: application/json
Authorization: Bearer <token>

{
    "student": "683f1a2b4c5d6e7f8a9b0c1d",
    "course":  "684a2c3d5e6f7a8b9c0d1e2f",
    "payment": "685b3d4e5f6a7b8c9d0e1f2a"
}

###

### ── MY COURSES ────────────────────────────────────────────────

### [8] View My Enrolled Courses
###     Returns all active enrollments for the logged-in student.
###     Each item includes the full course object + payment details.
###     Dropped enrollments and inactive courses are excluded.
GET http://localhost:1935/student-api/course
Authorization: Bearer <token>

###

### ── PROGRESS TRACKING ────────────────────────────────────────

### [9] Update Course Progress
###     progress: 0–100 integer.
###     Status auto-resolves: 0 → Enrolled, 1-99 → In Progress, 100 → Completed.
###     timeSpentMinutes is added to the running total (capped at 180 per call).
PATCH http://localhost:1935/student-api/course
Content-Type: application/json
Authorization: Bearer <token>

{
    "courseId": "684a2c3d5e6f7a8b9c0d1e2f",
    "progress": 35,
    "timeSpentMinutes": 45
}

###

### [10] Mark Course as Completed (progress = 100)
PATCH http://localhost:1935/student-api/course
Content-Type: application/json
Authorization: Bearer <token>

{
    "courseId": "684a2c3d5e6f7a8b9c0d1e2f",
    "progress": 100,
    "timeSpentMinutes": 60
}

###

### [11] Drop a Course
###      Sets status to "Dropped" — student leaves the course.
PATCH http://localhost:1935/student-api/course
Content-Type: application/json
Authorization: Bearer <token>

{
    "courseId": "684a2c3d5e6f7a8b9c0d1e2f",
    "status": "Dropped"
}

###

### [12] Mark a Chapter as Completed
###      Adds the chapterId to the completedChapter array in the enrollment.
###      Safe to call multiple times — duplicate entries are prevented.
PATCH http://localhost:1935/student-api/course/chapter-complete
Content-Type: application/json
Authorization: Bearer <token>

{
    "courseId": "684a2c3d5e6f7a8b9c0d1e2f",
    "chapterId": "685c4f5a6b7c8d9e0f1a2b3c"
}

###

### ── REVIEWS ───────────────────────────────────────────────────

### [13] Rate & Review a Course
###      rating: 1–5 (integer or decimal, validated server-side).
###      Student must be enrolled (not Dropped). One review per student per course.
PUT http://localhost:1935/student-api/course
Content-Type: application/json
Authorization: Bearer <token>

{
    "courseId": "684a2c3d5e6f7a8b9c0d1e2f",
    "rating": 5,
    "comment": "Excellent course! The instructor explains each concept clearly with real-world examples. Highly recommend to anyone starting with Java."
}

###

### ── WISHLIST ──────────────────────────────────────────────────

### [14] Get My Wishlist
###      Returns saved courses; inactive courses are filtered out automatically.
GET http://localhost:1935/student-api/wishlist
Authorization: Bearer <token>

###

### [15] Add a Course to Wishlist
###      Fails if the student is already enrolled. Idempotent — safe to call again.
POST http://localhost:1935/student-api/wishlist
Content-Type: application/json
Authorization: Bearer <token>

{
    "courseId": "684b3d4e5f6a7b8c9d0e1f3a"
}

###

### [16] Remove a Course from Wishlist
###      courseId goes in the URL path.
DELETE http://localhost:1935/student-api/wishlist/684b3d4e5f6a7b8c9d0e1f3a
Authorization: Bearer <token>

###

### ── DOUBTS ────────────────────────────────────────────────────

### [17] Get My Doubts
###      Returns all doubts posted by the logged-in student with full population:
###      matched peer, matched doubt details, instructor reply, peer answers.
GET http://localhost:1935/student-api/doubts
Authorization: Bearer <token>

###

### [18] Get Doubt Feed — All Enrolled Courses
###      Returns recent class-audience doubts from all enrolled courses (max 30).
###      Instructor-only doubts are excluded.
GET http://localhost:1935/student-api/doubts/feed
Authorization: Bearer <token>

###

### [19] Get Doubt Feed — Filtered by Course
###      Student must be enrolled in that course.
GET http://localhost:1935/student-api/doubts/feed?courseId=684a2c3d5e6f7a8b9c0d1e2f
Authorization: Bearer <token>

###

### [20] Post a Doubt to the Class
###      audience "class" — classmates can see and answer.
###      System auto-matches a similar doubt from the last 21 days (score ≥ 0.25).
###      status → "Matched" if a peer is found, else "Open".
POST http://localhost:1935/student-api/doubts
Content-Type: application/json
Authorization: Bearer <token>

{
    "courseId": "684a2c3d5e6f7a8b9c0d1e2f",
    "topic": "Difference between method overloading and overriding",
    "description": "I am confused about when to use overloading vs overriding in Java OOP. Can someone explain with a simple real-world example?",
    "audience": "class",
    "chapterTitle": "OOP Fundamentals",
    "unitTitle": "Inheritance and Polymorphism"
}

###

### [21] Post a Doubt to the Instructor
###      audience "instructor" — only the course instructor sees it.
###      Peer matching is skipped for instructor-directed doubts.
POST http://localhost:1935/student-api/doubts
Content-Type: application/json
Authorization: Bearer <token>

{
    "courseId": "684a2c3d5e6f7a8b9c0d1e2f",
    "topic": "Clarification on bounded wildcards in Generics",
    "description": "You used ? extends T and ? super T in the advanced chapter. I do not understand when to use each one. Could you provide a real-world analogy?",
    "audience": "instructor",
    "chapterTitle": "Advanced Java",
    "unitTitle": "Generics and Collections Framework"
}

###

### [22] Post a General Doubt (not linked to any course)
###      courseId is optional — the doubt is platform-wide.
POST http://localhost:1935/student-api/doubts
Content-Type: application/json
Authorization: Bearer <token>

{
    "topic": "Best approach for learning Data Structures?",
    "description": "I am preparing for placements and want to know the most effective order to learn arrays, linked lists, trees, and graphs. Should I start with theory or jump directly into coding problems?",
    "audience": "class"
}

###

### [23] Answer a Classmate's Doubt
###      Student must be enrolled in the same course as the doubt.
###      Posting an answer sets the doubt status to "Answered".
POST http://localhost:1935/student-api/doubts/684d1e2f3a4b5c6d7e8f9a0b/answers
Content-Type: application/json
Authorization: Bearer <token>

{
    "solution": "Overloading is compile-time polymorphism — same method name, different parameter types or count within the same class. Overriding is runtime polymorphism — redefining a parent-class method in the child class with the same signature. Use overloading for convenience variants; use overriding to change inherited behaviour."
}
